---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalHeader from '../components/LegalHeader.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <main class="bg-white">
    <LegalHeader lang="en" />
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 text-text">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-text-muted mb-10">
        <strong>Last updated:</strong> October 4, 2026
      </p>

      <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none space-y-8">
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">1. Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            This Privacy Policy is issued by <strong>Tenants10 KIG</strong>, Grütstrasse 28,
            8134 Adliswil, Switzerland (“Tenants10”, “we”, “us”, “our”), the controller
            responsible for the Tenants10 website, web application, and mobile applications
            (together, the “Service”), except where stated otherwise in Section 3 below.
          </p>
          <p>
            This Policy is written to comply with the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection
            (FADP, as revised, in force since 1 September 2023). Where a user or tenant is
            located in the European Economic Area, the relevant provisions of the EU General
            Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) apply in addition.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">2. Who this Policy covers</h2>
          <p>The Service is used by three kinds of people, and this Policy applies to all of them:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Staff users</strong> — employees of property management agencies, facility
              operators, contractors, and other business customers who hold an account on the
              platform.</li>
            <li><strong>Occupants / tenants</strong> — individuals living in or using a building
              managed through the Service (via the occupant portal or mobile app), invited by one
              of our business customers.</li>
            <li><strong>Visitors</strong> — people browsing tenants10.com without an account.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">3. Our role: controller vs. processor</h2>
          <p>
            For a <strong>staff user's own account data</strong> (login, profile, role, how they use
            the platform) and for <strong>visitors</strong> to our website, Tenants10 is the data
            controller.
          </p>
          <p>
            For <strong>occupant/tenant data</strong> entered into the platform by one of our
            business customers (an agency, landlord, or facility operator) — names, contact
            details, lease and payment records, maintenance requests, messages, documents, and
            similar — <strong>our business customer is the data controller</strong>, and Tenants10
            acts as their <strong>processor</strong>, handling that data only on their documented
            instructions and under a Data Processing Agreement (see Section 11). If you are an
            occupant/tenant and have a question about your data, please contact the property
            manager or organisation that invited you to the platform; they are responsible for
            responding to your request, and we support them in doing so.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">4. Information we collect</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Account & identity data:</strong> name, email, phone number, role, company,
              language preference, profile picture.</li>
            <li><strong>Property & tenancy data:</strong> building, unit, and lease information;
              rent and payment records; deposit information; maintenance and work order requests;
              inspection and compliance records.</li>
            <li><strong>Documents:</strong> contracts, floor plans, invoices, photos, and other
              files you or your organisation upload, stored in our document storage.</li>
            <li><strong>Communications:</strong> messages sent through the in-app chat, support
              tickets, and announcements, including their content.</li>
            <li><strong>Device & usage data:</strong> IP address, browser/device type, app version,
              push-notification tokens, log-in times, and general usage/diagnostic data.</li>
            <li><strong>Payment data:</strong> where billing is processed, payment method details
              are collected and stored directly by our payment processor (Stripe) — Tenants10 does
              not store full card numbers.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">5. How we use your information</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Provide, operate, and maintain the Service, including the occupant portal and
              mobile apps.</li>
            <li>Process rent payments, maintenance requests, bookings, and support requests.</li>
            <li>Send account, building, and service notifications (in-app, email, and push).</li>
            <li>Use AI (including Microsoft Azure OpenAI Service) to help extract and organise
              information from uploaded documents and to power in-app AI assistants — see Section 6.</li>
            <li>Automatically translate messages and notices between users who write in different
              languages (via Microsoft Azure Translator).</li>
            <li>Maintain platform security, detect abuse, and keep an audit trail of account
              activity.</li>
            <li>Comply with legal obligations, enforce our Terms of Service, and protect the
              rights and safety of our users.</li>
            <li>Improve the performance and reliability of the Service.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not use personal data for automated decision-making that produces legal or similarly significant effects, and we do not sell personal information.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">6. AI features</h2>
          <p>
            Certain features (such as document data extraction and AI assistants) send the
            relevant document or message content to Microsoft Azure OpenAI Service for
            processing. This is done under Microsoft's enterprise data-processing terms, which
            state that prompts and outputs sent through Azure OpenAI are not used to train
            Microsoft's or OpenAI's underlying models. AI-generated suggestions should be
            reviewed by a human before being relied upon for legal, financial, or safety-critical
            decisions.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">7. Who we share information with</h2>
          <p>We do not sell personal information. We share it only as needed to run the Service:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Within your organisation:</strong> staff users see occupant/tenant data
              according to the permissions their organisation assigns them.</li>
            <li><strong>Sub-processors (listed in Section 8)</strong> who host data, send
              notifications, process payments, or provide AI/translation features on our behalf,
              under written data-processing agreements.</li>
            <li><strong>Authorities</strong>, where required by Swiss law, a valid legal process,
              or to protect the rights, property, or safety of Tenants10, our users, or the public.</li>
            <li><strong>A successor entity</strong>, in the event of a merger, acquisition, or sale
              of assets, subject to the same data-protection commitments described here.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">8. Sub-processors & international transfers</h2>
          <p>
            Our primary infrastructure (application servers, database, and file storage) is
            hosted by <strong>Microsoft Azure in the Switzerland North region</strong>, meaning
            core platform data is stored in Switzerland. Some features rely on sub-processors
            that may process data outside Switzerland, in particular the United States:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Microsoft Azure</strong> (Switzerland North, with some AI/translation
              calls routed via Azure's regional endpoints) — hosting, database, file storage,
              document AI extraction, translation.</li>
            <li><strong>Google Firebase Cloud Messaging</strong> (United States) — delivery of
              mobile and browser push notifications. Push payloads are deliberately generic (a
              category label only — e.g. "New message" — never names, message content, or
              amounts) precisely because this channel crosses outside our own infrastructure.</li>
            <li><strong>Resend</strong> — transactional email delivery (account, notification,
              and password-reset emails).</li>
            <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — payment processing for platform subscriptions, where
              applicable.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Where personal data is transferred outside Switzerland or the EEA to a country
            without a recognised adequate level of data protection, we rely on the providers'
            standard contractual clauses and, where applicable, the EU–US / Swiss–US Data Privacy
            Framework, as the legal safeguard for that transfer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">9. Data retention</h2>
          <p>
            We retain personal data for as long as the related account or organisation is active
            on the Service, and for a reasonable period afterward to meet legal, accounting, and
            dispute-resolution obligations — generally up to 10 years for financial and contract
            records, consistent with Swiss retention requirements (Art. 958f CO). When an
            organisation closes its account, we delete or anonymise occupant/tenant personal data
            within a reasonable period, except where longer retention is required by law or
            agreed with that organisation under the Data Processing Agreement.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">10. Cookies & similar technologies</h2>
          <p>
            Our website and web application use cookies and similar local storage for essential
            functions (keeping you logged in, remembering preferences) and, where enabled,
            for analytics. See our <a href="/cookies" class="text-primary font-medium">Cookie Policy</a>
            for the full list and how to manage your choices.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">11. Data Processing Agreement (business customers)</h2>
          <p>
            If you are a business customer (an agency, landlord, or facility operator)
            processing your occupants'/tenants' personal data through the Service, our
            <a href="/dpa" class="text-primary font-medium">Data Processing Agreement</a> forms
            part of your contract with us and sets out the scope, purpose, sub-processors, and
            security measures that apply to that processing, as required under Art. 9 FADP.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">12. Data security</h2>
          <p>
            We use technical and organisational measures appropriate to the sensitivity of the
            data, including encryption in transit, role-based access control, audit logging, and
            regular review of third-party sub-processors. No method of transmission or storage is
            completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">13. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Under the FADP (and, where applicable, the GDPR), you have the right to request
            access to, correction of, deletion of, or restriction on the personal data we hold
            about you, and to object to certain processing. If your data was provided to us by
            your property manager or employer (see Section 3), please direct your request to
            them in the first instance; we will assist them in responding. You may also lodge a
            complaint with the <strong>Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner
            (FDPIC)</strong>, Feldeggweg 1, 3003 Bern, Switzerland (edoeb.admin.ch), or, if the
            GDPR applies to you, with your local EU data protection authority.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">14. Children</h2>
          <p>The Service is intended for business use and for adult occupants/tenants. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">15. Changes to this Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this Policy from time to time. Material changes will be announced in
            the app or by email to account holders, and the "Last updated" date above will be
            revised.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">16. Contact us</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about this Privacy Policy, or to exercise your rights, contact us at:
            <a href="mailto:support@tenants10.com" class="text-primary font-medium">
              support@tenants10.com
            </a>
            , or by post at Tenants10 KIG, Grütstrasse 28, 8134 Adliswil, Switzerland.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
